This project uses external tools without vendoring their implementations:
- NumPy: https://numpy.org/ (BSD-3-Clause)
- SciPy: https://scipy.org/ (BSD-3-Clause)
- scikit-fem: https://github.com/kinnala/scikit-fem (BSD-3-Clause)
  Optional tetrahedral basis, quadrature and variational-form assembly for 3D
  hyperelastic identification. The solver interface follows the total-Lagrangian
  workflow documented in the upstream hyperelasticity examples. No upstream
  implementation is vendored. Neo-Hookean elasticity is an established model.
- Matplotlib: https://matplotlib.org/ (Matplotlib license)
- pytest: https://pytest.org/ (MIT)
- JAX: https://github.com/jax-ml/jax (Apache-2.0)
- scikit-image: https://scikit-image.org/ (BSD-3-Clause), particle-surface reconstruction.
- PyOpenCL: https://github.com/inducer/pyopencl (MIT), access to the OpenCL runtime.
- PeriPy: https://github.com/alan-turing-institute/PeriPy (MIT)
  Copyright (c) 2020 Tim Dodwell.
  Optional source reference: 04cae072e22568e29b9ab8f84d821f9576ecb728.
  The unmodified peridynamics.cl and euler_cromer.cl kernels supply material
  forces, tensile bond failure and dynamics. The external checkout preserves
  its MIT license. SoftGripLab adds the moving-blade contact/cutting adapter.
- PyBullet / Bullet: https://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3 (zlib)
- Smooth sphere mesh supplied by pybullet_data/sphere_smooth.obj (Bullet zlib distribution).
- Panda robot asset supplied by pybullet_data/franka_panda (Apache-2.0).
  Original asset: bulletphysics/bullet3/examples/pybullet/gym/pybullet_data/franka_panda.
  The asset is loaded from the dependency, not vendored. Rendered robot frames
  show this upstream asset; its license is preserved in docs/licenses/FRANKA_PANDA.txt.
- JAX-MPM: https://github.com/lililii124/jax-mpm (GPL-3.0)
  Optional integration reference: fd8ed2caa40a50d01992420660f68ae6ce0d084f.
  The upstream solver itself preserves its own Taichi and other notices.
- DiSECt: https://github.com/NVlabs/DiSECt
  Optional research backend at ff90165070335bb8033000373d2d20c6aac13edd.
  NVIDIA Source Code License: research/evaluation restrictions apply separately.
  https://github.com/NVlabs/DiSECt/blob/main/LICENSE.md
  No DiSECt implementation or binary is bundled. The cutting adapter loads its
  knife geometry from the external backend; saved replay data includes that geometry.
  The default GPL installation does not install or import this backend.

The standard linear solid and Coulomb friction relations are established models.
SoftGripLab's contribution is the identification/grasp benchmark workflow,
validation cases, data conventions and adapter scene, not those constitutive laws.
